@lang en
IMPORT `vn14-ch5-claims-and-termination`

-- Tests for Chapter 2 (the tax paragraph, Articles 12 to 15). Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from what the SOURCE states, before the assertion was run; the working is beside each
-- group. A failing assertion is a finding, never a value to edit. The 12.3 table rows are tested
-- edge by edge in the generated vn14-tests-tables.l4; here they meet the other layers.

§ `Tests — Chapter 2`

§§ `Fixtures`

`the usual accounts` MEANS
    `The accounts` WITH
        `the Policyholder's account value`   IS 60_000_000
        `the Insured Member's account value` IS 40_000_000
        `the vesting ratio`                  IS 30%

GIVEN `plan` IS A `A Plan`
      `latest reinstatement date` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `state` IS A `A state of the part`
GIVETH AN `An Insured Member's part`
`a part on` `plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` `latest reinstatement date` `, now` `state` MEANS
    `An Insured Member's part` WITH
        `coverage start date`                    IS YMD 2020 1 1
        `maturity date`                          IS YMD 2040 1 1
        `latest reinstatement date`              IS `latest reinstatement date`
        `plan`                                   IS `plan`
        `sum insured`                            IS 1_000_000_000
        `sum insured at the coverage start date` IS 1_000_000_000
        `accounts`                               IS `the usual accounts`
        `debt`                                   IS 3_000_000
        `state`                                  IS `state`

`a Basic Plan part` MEANS `a part on` `the Basic Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` NOTHING `, now` `in force`
`an Enhanced Plan part` MEANS `a part on` `the Enhanced Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` NOTHING `, now` `in force`

-- A claim on an adult's death, varied by the facts the tests turn on. Fixed: born 1 January
-- 1980; claim received nine days after death; premium paid after the claim 5,000,000; Debt
-- 2,000,000; benefits paid after death 1,000,000; the Company's reasonable costs 1,000,000.
GIVEN `born` IS A DATE
      `died` IS A DATE
      `state` IS A `A state of the part`
      `sum insured` IS A NUMBER
      `account value` IS A NUMBER
      `funeral paid` IS A NUMBER
      `suicide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `crime by the Policyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`a death claim: born` `born` `, died` `died` `, part` `state` `, sum insured` `sum insured` `, account value` `account value` `, funeral paid` `funeral paid` `, suicide` `suicide` `, crime by the Policyholder` `crime by the Policyholder` MEANS
    `A death claim` WITH
        `date of birth of the Insured Member`              IS `born`
        `date of death`                                    IS `died`
        `date of the event causing death`                  IS `died`
        `date the Company received the death claim`        IS `died` PLUS 9
        `the Contract was in force at death`               IS TRUE
        `state of the part at death`                       IS `state`
        `sum insured at the time of death`                 IS `sum insured`
        `account value on the date the claim was received` IS `account value`
        `premium paid after the date of the death claim`   IS 5_000_000
        `funeral benefit already paid`                     IS `funeral paid`
        `benefits arising after death already paid`       IS 1_000_000
        `debt`                                             IS 2_000_000
        `reasonable costs incurred by the Company`         IS 1_000_000
        `suicide or a suicidal act, sane or insane`        IS `suicide`
        `a criminal act of the Insured Member`             IS FALSE
        `a criminal act of the Policyholder`               IS `crime by the Policyholder`
        `a criminal act of a Beneficiary`                  IS FALSE

GIVEN `died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`an ordinary adult death on` `died` MEANS
    `a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` `died` `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 30_000_000 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE

GIVEN `died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`a suicide on` `died` MEANS
    `a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` `died` `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` TRUE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE

§§ `Chapter 2 preamble — tax`

#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the payment` 100_000_000 `less the tax withheld of` 1_000_000 EQUALS 99_000_000

§§ `Article 12.1 — the funeral benefit`

-- Sum Insured 1,000,000,000: 10% is 100,000,000; the lesser with 30,000,000 is 30,000,000.
-- 200,000,000 -> 20,000,000. 300,000,000 -> 30,000,000 either way.
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit amount` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS 30_000_000
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit amount` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 200_000_000 `, account value` 10_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS 20_000_000
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit amount` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 300_000_000 `, account value` 10_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS 30_000_000
-- "after one (01) year" from 1 January 2020: payable from 1 January 2021 (fork F14).
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2021 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2020 12 31))
-- Reinstated 1 March 2025: the year restarts.
#ASSERT NOT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` (`a part on` `the Basic Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `, now` `in force`) `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` (`a part on` `the Basic Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `, now` `in force`) `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Excluded cause (a suicide on 1 June 2021, within two years): no funeral benefit.
#ASSERT NOT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2021 6 1))
-- The grace period counts as in force; a lapsed part does not.
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force, in the grace period` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `12.1 — the funeral benefit is payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `lapsed` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE)

§§ `Article 12.2 — the death benefit, each Plan`

-- Basic: the greater of 1,000,000,000 and 100,000,000; with an Account Value of
-- 1,200,000,000, that. Enhanced: 1,000,000,000 + 100,000,000.
#ASSERT `12.2 — the death benefit before 12.4, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `12.2 — the death benefit before 12.4, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 1_200_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS 1_200_000_000
#ASSERT `12.2 — the death benefit before 12.4, for` `an Enhanced Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS 1_100_000_000

§§ `Article 12.4 — the adjustments`

-- Basic: 1,000,000,000 + 5,000,000 premium after the claim - 2,000,000 Debt - 30,000,000 funeral
-- already paid - 1,000,000 benefits after death = 972,000,000.
#ASSERT `12.4 — the death benefit payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS 972_000_000
-- Enhanced: 1,100,000,000 + 5 - 2 - 30 - 1 (millions) = 1,072,000,000.
#ASSERT `12.4 — the death benefit payable, for` `an Enhanced Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS 1_072_000_000

§§ `Article 12.3 — a child, through every layer`

-- Born 1 June 2024, died 15 January 2026: 19 completed months -> 40%. Sum Insured 500,000,000
-- -> 200,000,000. Funeral: the lesser of 10% (20,000,000) and 30,000,000 = 20,000,000.
-- Basic: the greater of 200,000,000 and 10,000,000. Then 12.4 with 20,000,000 funeral paid:
-- 200 + 5 - 2 - 20 - 1 = 182,000,000.
`a child's death` MEANS
    `a death claim: born` (YMD 2024 6 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 500_000_000 `, account value` 10_000_000 `, funeral paid` 20_000_000 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE

#ASSERT `12.3 — the Sum Insured for 12.1 and 12.2, adjusted for a child, under` `a child's death` EQUALS 200_000_000
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit amount` `a child's death` EQUALS 20_000_000
#ASSERT `12.2 — the death benefit before 12.4, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` `a child's death` EQUALS 200_000_000
#ASSERT `12.4 — the death benefit payable, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` `a child's death` EQUALS 182_000_000
-- Enhanced, the same child: 200,000,000 + 10,000,000 = 210,000,000; 12.4: 210 + 5 - 2 - 20 - 1 = 192,000,000.
#ASSERT `12.4 — the death benefit payable, for` `an Enhanced Plan part` `and` `a child's death` EQUALS 192_000_000
-- On the fourth birthday the table no longer applies: born 15 January 2022, died 15 January 2026.
#ASSERT `12.3 — the Sum Insured for 12.1 and 12.2, adjusted for a child, under` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 2022 1 15) `, died` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 500_000_000 `, account value` 10_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS 500_000_000
#ASSERT `12.3 — the Sum Insured for 12.1 and 12.2, adjusted for a child, under` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 2022 1 16) `, died` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 500_000_000 `, account value` 10_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS 400_000_000

§§ `Article 15 — each exclusion, with its near miss`

-- (a) suicide within two years of 1 January 2020: 31 December 2021 is inside; 1 January 2022,
-- the second anniversary, is outside (fork F13).
#ASSERT `15 — the death is excluded, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2021 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT `15 — the death is excluded, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2022 1 1))
-- Reinstated 1 March 2023: a suicide on 1 June 2024 is inside the new two years.
#ASSERT `15 — the death is excluded, for` (`a part on` `the Basic Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2023 3 1)) `, now` `in force`) `and` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2024 6 1))
-- (b) a criminal act of the Policyholder; its near miss is the ordinary death.
#ASSERT `15 — the death is excluded, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `15 — the death is excluded, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1))
-- What is paid instead: 100,000,000 - 1,000,000 costs - 0 funeral - 2,000,000 Debt = 97,000,000.
#ASSERT `15 — the account value paid instead` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2021 12 31)) EQUALS 97_000_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `15 — the account value paid instead` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2021 5 1) `, part` `in force` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 1_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` TRUE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE)

§§ `Chapter 2 — the outcome, through every layer`

#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`an ordinary adult death on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 12, net under 12.4, of` 972_000_000
#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2021 12 31)) EQUALS `only the account value under Article 15, of` 97_000_000
#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `lapsed` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS `no benefit: the part had lapsed or terminated`
#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `suspended` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS `no benefit: the part was suspended under Article 20`
-- In the grace period the part is in force (18.1): 1,000,000,000 + 5 - 2 - 0 - 1 (millions).
#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part` `and` (`a death claim: born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, part` `in force, in the grace period` `, sum insured` 1_000_000_000 `, account value` 100_000_000 `, funeral paid` 0 `, suicide` FALSE `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 12, net under 12.4, of` 1_002_000_000

§§ `Article 13 — the maturity benefit`

#ASSERT `13 — the maturity benefit is payable on the Maturity Date of` `a Basic Plan part`
#ASSERT NOT `13 — the maturity benefit is payable on the Maturity Date of` (`a part on` `the Basic Plan` `from 1 January 2020, last reinstated` NOTHING `, now` `lapsed`)
-- 100,000,000 less Debt 3,000,000; the split 42,000,000 / 58,000,000 before Debt.
#ASSERT `13 — the total maturity benefit of` `a Basic Plan part` EQUALS 97_000_000
#ASSERT (`13 — the maturity benefit split, before Debt, of` `a Basic Plan part`) EQUALS (`A split between the Policyholder and the Insured Member` WITH `to the Policyholder` IS 42_000_000, `to the Insured Member` IS 58_000_000)

§§ `Article 14 — the loyalty bonus`

GIVEN `anniversary` IS A NUMBER
      `kept in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `withdrew` IS A BOOLEAN
      `current sum insured` IS A NUMBER
      `values` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `A loyalty bonus review`
`a review at anniversary` `anniversary` `, kept in force` `kept in force` `, paid in full` `paid in full` `, withdrew` `withdrew` `, sum insured now` `current sum insured` `, values` `values` MEANS
    `A loyalty bonus review` WITH
        `Policy Anniversary number`                                      IS `anniversary`
        `in force and never lapsed or suspended in the review period`    IS `kept in force`
        `premium paid in full for every instalment in the review period` IS `paid in full`
        `any account value withdrawal in the review period`              IS `withdrew`
        `current sum insured`                                            IS `current sum insured`
        `sum insured at the coverage start date`                         IS 1_000_000_000
        `account values at the last 60 Monthly Anniversaries`            IS `values`

-- Sixty values of 100,000,000: average 100,000,000, 5% = 5,000,000.
-- Sixty values of 1,000,000 x (1..60): average 30,500,000, 5% = 1,525,000.
`sixty flat values` MEANS map (GIVEN n YIELD 100_000_000) (`the numbers from 1 to` 60)
`sixty rising values` MEANS map (GIVEN n YIELD n TIMES 1_000_000) (`the numbers from 1 to` 60)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the numbers from 1 to` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0 THEN EMPTY ELSE append (`the numbers from 1 to` (n MINUS 1)) (LIST n)

#ASSERT `14.1 — a review period closes at Policy Anniversary number` 5
#ASSERT NOT `14.1 — a review period closes at Policy Anniversary number` 4
#ASSERT NOT `14.1 — a review period closes at Policy Anniversary number` 6
#ASSERT `14.1 — a review period closes at Policy Anniversary number` 10
#ASSERT NOT `14.1 — a review period closes at Policy Anniversary number` 0
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 5_000_000
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 10 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_200_000_000 `, values` `sixty rising values`) EQUALS 1_525_000
-- Each condition, failed alone, with the passing case above as its near miss.
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` FALSE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` TRUE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 999_999_999 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 6 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` `sixty flat values`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `14.1 — the loyalty bonus credited` (`a review at anniversary` 5 `, kept in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, withdrew` FALSE `, sum insured now` 1_000_000_000 `, values` (`the numbers from 1 to` 59))
-- 14.3: 5,000,000 shared 60:40 -> 3,000,000 and 2,000,000.
#ASSERT (`14.3 — the bonus` 5_000_000 `shared between the accounts` `the usual accounts`) EQUALS (`A split between the Policyholder and the Insured Member` WITH `to the Policyholder` IS 3_000_000, `to the Insured Member` IS 2_000_000)
#ASSERT REFUSED `14.3 — the bonus` 5_000_000 `shared between the accounts` (`The accounts` WITH `the Policyholder's account value` IS 0, `the Insured Member's account value` IS 0, `the vesting ratio` IS 0)
